al, and was disqualified."] "\n\n" [:p {} "However, even without the penalty, Germany did not win the race.  Great Britain held them off, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/68844"} "Willie Applegarth"] " refusing to allow " [:a {:href "/athletes/70456"} "Richard Rau"] " to pass him in the final straight.  Both were timed in 42.4, as Britain won by a few centimetres.  After the German disqualification, Sweden was awarded the silver medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "45.0 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "43.0 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "42.4 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/69189"} "David Jacobs"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/69269"} "Henry Macintosh"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/68998"} "Vic d'Arcy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/68844"} "Willie Applegarth"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "43.6 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "42.5 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "42.6 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/76314"} "Ivan Möller"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/76293"} "Karl August Luther"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/76351"} "Ture Persson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/76261"} "Knut Lindberg"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "AC r3/3"] [:td {} "Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/count